    "units_correction": {
      "finding": "The earlier label 'per source particle, cm' was wrong. Those runs set the source strength to 1.8618e20 n/s, and OpenMC multiplies fixed-source tallies by the total source strength, so the stored 1.78e17 is a rate in n.cm/s at 525 MW. The score is a track length (OpenMC 'flux' is particle-cm, not divided by volume). Divided by the rate it is 9.55e-4 cm per source neutron (0.15.3) and 8.09e-4 (0.16.0), summed over 18 TF coils above 0.1 MeV.",
      "hand_check": "Same model, strength 1, 5x2000 histories: plasma-cell track length 680 cm per source neutron; strength 1.8618e20 gives 1.267e23, ratio exactly 1.8618e20. Order check: mean isotropic chord 4V/S with V=1.457e8 cm3 and S ~ 1.8e6 cm2 is about 330 cm for a first flight; scattering returns from the first wall roughly double it, consistent with 680 cm.",
      "from_now_on": "R1 to R3 runs use strength 1 and report 'cm per source neutron'; rates are produced only through rm_m_checks.to_rate."
    }
